    {
      "id": "G001",
      "gap": "Lack of deterministic, non-heuristic optimal algorithms for solving the trimmed k-means problem across general parameter spaces.",
      "why_it_matters": "Because no deterministic algorithm guarantees global optimality for trimmed k-means, practitioners must rely on heuristic optimization (such as simulated annealing), making solutions sensitive to initialization and stopping criteria.",
      "what_is_known": "The existence of trimmed k-means and their asymptotic consistency has been established theoretically under continuity conditions, and heuristic tools (like simulated annealing and FAST-MCD variants) can compute them in practice.",
      "what_remains_unknown": "Whether a computationally feasible, deterministic algorithm can be designed to find the exact optimal trimmed partition without depending on stochastic search heuristics.",
